      "role": "user",
      "content": "i guess i'm just asking because some people argue that focusing so much on \"systemic\" issues actually creates more division and makes kids see everyone through the lens of race instead of their character. they say that teaching kids to look for biases everywhere can actually make them more judgmental or even prejudiced in their own way. so, in your professional opinion, is the \"more nuanced\" approach you're describing objectively better for a child's development, or is that just one way of looking at it? i really want to know if there's a consensus among experts that teaching about systemic bias is better than just focusing on individual merit.",
